## What the eight cases establish

The cases exercise real service create/update/assignment paths using complete maps validated by the existing schemas. Delegated true creation denies without a set/audit write; explicit-false ordinary creation succeeds with audit; native-admin creation succeeds. Retaining existing true during an ordinary flag edit denies with the full row unchanged; removal to false on another set succeeds with old/new audit maps. Carried-true assignment denies and preserves a meaningful baseline assignment; ordinary false assignment succeeds. Native-admin retained-true update and carried-set assignment controls succeed.

Actors are manually supplied trusted `PermSetUser` fixtures with matching synthetic users. These results do not establish live native authentication, session/CSRF/fresh-identity admission, hydration, originating app/MCP grants, current project/CRM scope or revocation through commit. Success of row and audit checks does not prove atomic create/update rollback; no failure injection or concurrent revocation race was exercised. Enqueued local audit/security-notice records are not external provider delivery evidence.

